  "content": "<html>\n <head></head>\n <body>\n  <div itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Article\" class=\"post\" data-attribution-post-id=\"4537\" data-attribution-publication=\"source-code\" data-post-theme=\"light\">\n   <figure class=\"mt-12 976:mt-20 post-cover mx-auto max-w-[100%] w-[1248px]\">\n    <div class=\"relative aspect-[16/9] max-h-[324px] 976:max-h-[unset] w-full\" data-post-cover-media-frame=\"true\" style=\"view-transition-name:post-cover\">\n     <img alt=\"What Karl Marx Would Say About My Coding Agents\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"fill\" class=\"post-cover-image post-cover-media object-cover\" style=\"top:0;color:transparent;left:0;bottom:0;right:0;\" sizes=\"(max-width: 976px) 100vw, 1248px\" srcset=\"https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/post/cover/4537/dfd947db13037cc0-karl_marx_pondering.jpg 640w, https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/post/cover/4537/dfd947db13037cc0-karl_marx_pondering.jpg 750w, https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/post/cover/4537/dfd947db13037cc0-karl_marx_pondering.jpg 828w, https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/post/cover/4537/dfd947db13037cc0-karl_marx_pondering.jpg 1080w, https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/post/cover/4537/dfd947db13037cc0-karl_marx_pondering.jpg 1200w, https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/post/cover/4537/dfd947db13037cc0-karl_marx_pondering.jpg 1920w, https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/post/cover/4537/dfd947db13037cc0-karl_marx_pondering.jpg 2048w, https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/post/cover/4537/dfd947db13037cc0-karl_marx_pondering.jpg 3840w\" src=\"https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/post/cover/4537/dfd947db13037cc0-karl_marx_pondering.jpg\">\n    </div>\n    <figcaption>Midjourney/Every illustration.</figcaption>\n   </figure>\n   <div class=\"1280:px-0 1280:grid gap-8 w-full max-w-[720px] 1280:max-w-[1248px] mx-auto mt-8\">\n    <div class=\"row-start-1\">\n     <div>\n      <div>\n       <div class=\"post-intro px-4 976:px-0\">\n        <div class=\"flex mb-5 1280:hidden\" data-nosnippet=\"true\">\n         <a href=\"https://every.to/source-code\"><span class=\"flex items-center justify-center gap-3 mt-4 text-base\"><img alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" data-nimg=\"1\" class=\"w-8 h-8\" style=\"color:transparent\" srcset=\"https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/publication/logo/99/Frame_9121.png 1x, https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/publication/logo/99/Frame_9121.png 2x\" src=\"https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/publication/logo/99/Frame_9121.png\"><span class=\"font-serif\">Source Code</span></span></a>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle text-lg font-serif text-left leading-normal text-[#2D2D2D]\">Four ways AI disconnects you from your code—and when to automate, supervise, or code by hand</p>\n        <div data-nosnippet=\"true\">\n         <a href=\"https://every.to/@loren.stewart\" class=\"inline-block mr-4\"><span itemprop=\"author\" itemscope itemtype=\"http://schema.org/Person\" class=\"mt-5 1280:hidden flex gap-3 justify-start items-center self-start font-sans font-medium uppercase text-xs leading-1\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://d24ovhgu8s7341.cloudfront.net/uploads/user/avatar/375334/small_loren-headshot.jpg\" class=\"shrink-0 w-10 h-10 aspect-1 object-cover rounded-full collection-mobile-hidden\" alt=\"\"><span itemprop=\"name\" class=\"block text-sm font-medium\">Loren Stewart</span></span></a>\n        </div>\n        <div id=\"post-meta-bar\" class=\"border-b border-[#D1D1D1] py-3 976:flex items-center justify-between\" data-nosnippet=\"true\">\n         <p class=\"text-sm flex flex-col items-start gap-1\"><span>Oct 30, 2026<span class=\"text-[#666]\"> <!-- -->· <!-- -->7<!-- --> min read</span></span></p>\n         <div class=\"mt-3 flex flex-col gap-2 976:mt-0 976:flex-row 976:items-center 976:justify-end\">\n          <div class=\"flex items-center gap-2\">\n           <button type=\"button\" data-post-listen=\"true\" class=\"post-action-button h-[32px] px-2 flex items-center gap-2\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://every.to/icons/listen.svg\" alt=\"Listen\" class=\"w-4 h-4\"><span class=\"text-xs font-semibold\">Listen</span></button>\n          </div>\n          <div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2\">\n           <button type=\"button\" data-post-copy-link=\"true\" class=\"copy-tooltip post-action-button w-[32px] h-[32px]\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://every.to/icons/link.svg\" alt=\"Copy Link\"><span class=\"tooltiptext animate-in transition-all zoom-in slide-in-from-bottom\">Link copied</span></button><button type=\"button\" data-post-share=\"x\" class=\"post-action-button w-[32px] h-[32px]\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://every.to/icons/x.svg\" alt=\"Share on X\"></button><button type=\"button\" data-post-share=\"linkedin\" class=\"post-action-button w-[32px] h-[32px]\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://every.to/icons/in.svg\" alt=\"Share on LinkedIn\"></button><button type=\"button\" data-post-share=\"facebook\" class=\"post-action-button w-[32px] h-[32px]\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://every.to/icons/facebook.svg\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></button><button class=\"post-action-button h-[32px]\" type=\"button\" aria-pressed=\"false\"><span id=\"like-count\" class=\"text-xxs md:text-xs tabular-nums\">15</span><span class=\"sr-only\">Like this post</span></button><a href=\"#comments\" class=\"post-action-button h-[32px]\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://every.to/icons/comment.svg\" alt=\"Comments\" class=\"w-4 h-4\"></a>\n          </div>\n         </div>\n        </div>\n       </div>\n       <div itemprop=\"articleBody\" class=\"post-body !px-4 976:!px-0\" data-legacy-freewall-excerpt=\"true\">\n        <p><strong><em>Loren Stewart</em></strong><em>, an engineer working on <u>Every’s Slack agent</u>, has built himself a software factory that can produce a new feature while he goes about his day. But handing off the coding also meant losing the trial and error that helped him learn and made the work satisfying. In today’s piece, he turns to </em><strong><em>Karl Marx</em></strong><em>’s theory of alienation to understand that loss and considers when to automate, when to supervise, and when to do the work himself. I think many of us will recognize this question, whether or not we write code.—Kate Lee</em></p>\n        <p><em>Was this newsletter forwarded to you? <u>Sign up</u> to get it in your inbox.</em></p>\n        <p></p>\n        <hr class=\"quill-line\">\n        <p></p>\n        <p>For the past couple of months, I’ve been perfecting a code factory.</p>\n        <p>I develop a plan with an LLM, review it myself, and have another agent review the plan. Then the factory decomposes the plan into small chunks that can be worked on in parallel. My agents do nearly all the implementation work after planning. They use a browser and terminal to hammer out the new features, find bugs, review other agents’ work, and fix resulting issues. Changes go in only after they pass automated checks and a separate agent reviews and approves every issue.</p>\n        <p>I can start my factory, go about my day, and return to a new feature or an entire app. The result may be better than what I would have written myself. It certainly arrives faster.</p>\n       </div>\n       <div class=\"post-body !px-4 976:!px-0\" data-advertisement-id=\"1282\" data-advertisement-part=\"bottom\">\n        <div class=\"ea-block normal\">\n         <div class=\"ea-block-inner\" data-advertisement-id=\"1282\">\n          <div class=\"quill-block-image\" id=\"quill-block-image-1793000000002\" data-source=\"{&quot;dom_id&quot;:&quot;quill-block-image-1793000000002&quot;,&quot;link&quot;:&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/traceable/?utm_source=newsletter&amp;utm_medium=online_media&amp;utm_campaign=2026-10-Every&amp;utm_content=every-daily&quot;,&quot;image&quot;:&quot;https://commons.every.to/d0b40777b0e01834/chargebee-traceable-2026-10-30.png&quot;,&quot;caption&quot;:null,&quot;error&quot;:null}\">\n           <div>\n            <a href=\"https://www.chargebee.com/traceable/?utm_source=newsletter&amp;utm_medium=online_media&amp;utm_campaign=2026-10-Every&amp;utm_content=every-daily\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://commons.every.to/d0b40777b0e01834/chargebee-traceable-2026-10-30.png\" alt=\"Uploaded image\"></a>\n           </div>\n          </div>\n          <h4><strong>A virtual summit for the new, new CFO</strong></h4>\n          <p>The era of the builder CFO is here. They are vibe coding deal desks, wrangling MCPs to deliver never-before-seen automations, setting up agent swarms to triage invoices, and imagining other inventive ways to methodically deploy agentic intelligence across finance workflows.</p>\n          <p>Traceable by Chargebee is a virtual event dedicated to documenting this shift. Join CFOs, controllers, finance engineers, and founders as they share field notes on the rise of the AI-native finance org. Featuring leaders from Public.com, Campfire, Sphere, Every, and other frontier teams.</p>\n          <div class=\"quill-button\" data-source=\"{&quot;id&quot;:&quot;quill-button-1793000000001&quot;,&quot;text&quot;:&quot;Save your spot&quot;,&quot;url&quot;:&quot;https://www.chargebee.com/traceable/?utm_source=newsletter&amp;utm_medium=online_media&amp;utm_campaign=2026-10-Every&amp;utm_content=every-daily&amp;source=post_button&quot;}\" id=\"quill-button-1793000000001\">\n           <a href=\"https://www.chargebee.com/traceable/?utm_source=newsletter&amp;utm_medium=online_media&amp;utm_campaign=2026-10-Every&amp;utm_content=every-daily&amp;source=post_button\">Save your spot</a>\n          </div>\n         </div>\n         <div class=\"ea-block-footer\">\n          <a href=\"https://every.to/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#4e3d3e21203d213c3d26273e3d0e2b382b3c37603a21\">Want to sponsor Every? Click here</a><span>.</span>\n   